// EXPECT-DIAG: E076
// EXPECT-DIAG: Integer literal is not representable in type 'int'
// SEM-003 (§11.6, the §20 worked example): proves SEM-001 -> SEM-002 ->
// SEM-003 compose correctly. §11.6 is explicit that the DEFAULT type is
// chosen first (int, for an untyped integer literal) and representability
// is checked AGAINST THAT DEFAULT second -- so this must be the ordinary
// SEM-002 out-of-range error against 'int', never a promotion to some wider
// type (there is no wider integer type, FREEZE.md §6.2). Falls out of
// TypeChecker::visitVarDecl reusing the pre-existing
// checkLiteralRepresentable() call after guess resolves DeclTy = InitTy,
// with no guess-specific representability code at all.
fn main(): int {
    mut x = 999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999;
    return 0;
}
